  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A set of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> tuning forks is arranged in a series of increasing frequencies. If each fork gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> beats with respect to the preceding fork and the frequency of the last fork is twice the frequency of the first, then the frequency of last fork is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "152",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0e711a64-cc9b-499a-8e8f-b9b7ea69c01e-image.png\" style=\"width: 326px; height: 90px;\" /></p><p>Each fork produces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;beats per second with the previous means each fork has frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> more than the previous.</p><p>Using relation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>last</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>first</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the number of tuning fork in series and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;beat frequency between two successive forks.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>76</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Frequency of last tuning fork is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>152</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
